module-oss (illumos): a card per device, holding the output ports.
libgnome-volume-control (GNOME Shell's volume menu, Settings > Sound) makes
an output entry for a sink with ports only through a port of its card, so
the ports added in patch 31 made every OSS output vanish from GNOME. Now
each device with output ports gets a card "oss_card.dspN" with one output
profile, the ports move onto the card and the sink refers to them, as
module-alsa-card does. Digital devices (one per GPU) are numbered after
their dsp node ("HDMI / DisplayPort Audio 2") until the codec reports the
monitor's ELD.
OpenIndiana project, 2026.

